Author:     Pavel Kudrevatykh <p.kudrevatyh@partner.samsung.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Aug 18 19:07:40 2025 +0300
Commit:     Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com>
CommitDate: Wed Jul 22 21:31:22 2026 +0900

    Fix armv7l build when compiler is clang
    
    By default, compiler_rt for armv7l is built with flag -mfloat-abi=soft.
    In prjconfig we specify flag -mfloat-abi=softfp.
    For gcc this doesn't cause problems, but for clang it causes error "no fp registers".
    Also, libraries of compiler_rt are built for arm and armv4t, which is redundant.
    
    Change arch and flags for arm.
    Define correctly CMAKE_ASM_FLAGS.
    
    Change-Id: Ic3dd8c37054a106262171d6a82fe00911ef45245
    (cherry picked from commit 9b5cb26fefe3e6ec60be09d298f388ea5f75595e)

